{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T10:09:32.174171", "data": {"url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/arindam-barman-3a480153_my-father-in-laws-thoughts-on-meeting-ratan-activity-7250176816844292096-Mowd", "title": "My father in law's thoughts on meeting Ratan Tata back in the day. | Arindam Barman", "content": "Arindam Barman\u2019s Post Arindam Barman 1y Report this post My father in law's thoughts on meeting Ratan Tata back in the day. Richa Goswami 1y Edited Reposting my Father Pulak Goswami's thoughts- There are a few losses that feel personal and today Sri Ratan Tata's death feels like that to me. Have known Sri Ratan Tata through the years. Back when I was a Tata Motors dealer, I had numerous occasions of meeting Sri Tata and had various fruitful interactions with him. In fact, he knew me on a first-name basis and called me Pulak. I remember once back in 2005 or 2006 maybe, I had sent a New Year card to Sri Ratan Tata. Never expected any reply, but a few days later when I received a Thank you letter personally from him, I knew why he was the person he was. He was the man behind Tata Motors. Back in 1998, when it was known as Telco. From thinking of selling the company in 1999 to Ford to today where it stands, Sri Ratan Tata is the reason for the company's growth. In fact his belief in the company is what inspired me to be a dealer in 1999. Those years in Tata Motors with Sri Tata were some of my most cherished memories. One of the most special days of my life would be when Sri Ratan Tata visited my office back in August 2011 and spent the whole day with us. It was raining heavily so we thought the program would be cancelled. But we had planned the whole program and I had thought of inaugurating my head office by Him. Although the program got delayed, but he made it and spent such beautiful times with all of us. I remember when I invited him to light the lamp first, he insisted that my mother should be one to light it first. Such was his humility. He is the one and all of the company but he still manages to connect with all the stakeholders- be his dealers or customers. During his visit to our office, he managed to meet all the customers who came and also greeted all my employees. His greatness with humility is the one aspect that has inspired me the most and I have tried to inculcate that in my work life as well. After his visit in 2011, next when he visited Guwahati, as he could not visit my office, he sent a personal mail to me sending his best wishes and that he would not be able to visit my office but next time he would try again. such was his greatness !! His greatness with humility is the one aspect that has inspired me the most and I have tried to inculcate that in my work life as well. Today, I along with the whole of India stand with our heads bowed down before him paying our respects for his final journey. There won't be a second Ratan Tata. He indeed is our \"Bharat Ratan\". #ratantata #tatagroup +6 22 Like Comment Share Copy LinkedIn Facebook X To view or add a comment, sign in 2,842 followers 138 Posts View Profile Follow Explore content categories Career Productivity Finance Soft Skills & Emotional Intelligence Project Management Education Technology Leadership Ecommerce User Experience Show more Show less Arindam Barman 1y Report this post My father in law's thoughts on meeting Ratan Tata back in the day. Richa Goswami 1y Edited Reposting my Father Pulak Goswami's thoughts- There are a few losses that feel personal and today Sri Ratan Tata's death feels like that to me. Have known Sri Ratan Tata through the years. Back when I was a Tata Motors dealer, I had numerous occasions of meeting Sri Tata and had various fruitful interactions with him. In fact, he knew me on a first-name basis and called me Pulak. I remember once back in 2005 or 2006 maybe, I had sent a New Year card to Sri Ratan Tata. Never expected any reply, but a few days later when I received a Thank you letter personally from him, I knew why he was the person he was. He was the man behind Tata Motors. Back in 1998, when it was known as Telco. From thinking of selling the company in 1999 to Ford to today where it stands, Sri Ratan Tata is the reason for the company's growth. In fact his belief in the company is what inspired me to be a dealer in 1999. Those years in Tata Motors with Sri Tata were some of my most cherished memories. One of the most special days of my life would be when Sri Ratan Tata visited my office back in August 2011 and spent the whole day with us. It was raining heavily so we thought the program would be cancelled. But we had planned the whole program and I had thought of inaugurating my head office by Him. Although the program got delayed, but he made it and spent such beautiful times with all of us. I remember when I invited him to light the lamp first, he insisted that my mother should be one to light it first. Such was his humility. He is the one and all of the company but he still manages to connect with all the stakeholders- be his dealers or customers. During his visit to our office, he managed to meet all the customers who came and also greeted all my employees. His greatness with humility is the one aspect that has inspired me the most and I have tried to inculcate that in my work life as well. After his visit in 2011, next when he visited Guwahati, as he could not visit my office, he sent a personal mail to me sending his best wishes and that he would not be able to visit my office but next time he would try again. such was his greatness !! His greatness with humility is the one aspect that has inspired me the most and I have tried to inculcate that in my work life as well. Today, I along with the whole of India stand with our heads bowed down before him paying our respects for his final journey. There won't be a second Ratan Tata. He indeed is our \"Bharat Ratan\". #ratantata #tatagroup +6 22 Like Comment Share Copy LinkedIn Facebook X To view or add a comment, sign in Arindam Barm